==Trivia==
*She is quite literally a [[wikipedia:Sea angel|sea angel]], a creature known for its grace, beauty and horror, seen in [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xlc7r34Sh-c this video].
*Her gender is confirmed by the [[Media:ClionelPoster.jpg|event poster]] for Clionel Ascendant, which says, "Can you withstand her as she rains fire from long distance?!" Clionel is also called a mother (엄마 ''eomma'') in her Korean description.
*Among the first seven [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]], Cruel Angel Clionel appears to represent the sin of wrath, as the [[Media:Clionel Ascendant poster JP.jpg|Japanese event poster]] for [[No Plan A (Deadly)|Clionel Ascendant]] says she "thoroughly burns everything" (全てを焼き尽す).
**Alternatively, Clionel could be symbolic of the eighth Deadly Sin, despair/despond, as "No Plan A" is a name that greatly suggests hopelessness. This would leave [[Kappy Jr.]] as wrath.
*Cruel Angel Clionel makes several references to ''[[wikipedia:Neon Genesis Evangelion|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]'':
**Her title is a reference to the name of the main theme of ''Neon Genesis Evangelion'', "[[wikia:evangelion:A Cruel Angel's Thesis|A Cruel Angel's Thesis]]", while the first sentence of her description states the main plot of the anime ([https://wiki.evageeks.org/Human_Instrumentality_Project Human Instrumentality Project], also known as [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Third_Impact Third Impact]).
**Her Japanese description incorporates the wordplay from [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Episode_24 Episode 24]:「最後のシ者」 The Beginning and the End. The specific borrowed term (シ者 ''shisha'') can be read in three different ways, either as envoy, casualty or on the water's edge. Presumably this enemy is all three at once.
**No Plan A's Japanese name, Neko Hokan Keikaku (ネコ補完計画, "Cat Complementary Project") is a reference to the Japanese name of the Human Instrumentality Project, Jinrui Hokan Keikaku (人類補完計画, "Human Complementary Project").
**[[A Cat Screaming Love (Merciless)|A Cat Screaming Love]]'s name comes from ''[[wikipedia:The Beast that Shouted Love at the Heart of the World (short story)|The Beast that Shouted Love at the Heart of the World]]'', a story by Harlan Ellison, and—more relevantly—the title of [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Episode_26 Episode 26] of ''Neon Genesis Evangelion''.
**Her attack animation shows several cross-shaped explosions - a common theme in Neon Genesis Evangelion.
*By hacking to make [[Kung-Fu X Awakens!|event map 1091]] appear before it was fully implemented, Clionel could once be fought alongside [[Gentleman Bros. (Enemy)|Gentleman Bros.]] in an [https://youtube.com/watch?v=Sxgc-WCp-bA unfinished stage] with the placeholder name その１ (''Sono 1'', lit. "Part 1"), which later became [[Old Master (Expert)]].
*In both [[The Battle Cats]] and [[The Battle Cats Unite!|The Battle Cats Unite]], Clionel was the first ever Advent Boss.

